(Ashgrove Regional Transit - Operations and Employee Manual - 2027 Edition) Tj T* T*
T*
/F2 14 Tf
(5.1 Procedure SR-402: Flooded roads) Tj T* T*
/F1 10 Tf
/F1 10 Tf
(Under procedure SR-402: Do not enter standing water deeper than 15 centimetres.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Also under procedure SR-402: Report the location to the control room and wait for a diversion) Tj T*
(instruction.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Every employee must know where this procedure applies and must follow it without waiting for) Tj T*
(instructions when immediate action is needed. As soon as it is safe to do so, tell the control) Tj T*
(room what has happened, where you are, and whether anyone has been hurt.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(The control room records the time of the call and decides whether to send a supervisor, stop other) Tj T*
(services, or contact the emergency services. Do not speak to the media or post about the event on) Tj T*
(social media. Refer all questions to the communications team.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(After the event, the depot safety officer reviews what happened and decides whether a formal) Tj T*
(investigation is required under Part 8. Lessons learned are shared at the next depot safety) Tj T*
(meeting so that other teams can benefit from them.) Tj T*
T*
/F1 10 Tf
(Employees are protected from blame when they stop work in good faith because they believed there) Tj T*
(was a serious risk. Concerns can also be raised confidentially with any safety officer or through) Tj T*
(the staff portal.) Tj T*
T*
ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 280 24 Td (Page 56 of 100) Tj ET
endstream
